# L §5.10 Parts (2.1-F10): "the sign rule is not checked against a hole balance, as in 2.0" (E §4.2 step 5); L §5.14
# A hole in a term: "Only the parts the take could reach under some reading of the holes merge"; L §8.1 (2.1-F12) "a
# part whose every possible label is q's is read as q's".  The migrator's F-h (fh_hole_outflow): acc, owned and min 0,
# gets 100.00 (ania_tomek's by the community rule), then sp takes the hole amount spend, then fix takes a fixed 150.00.
# The balance after sp is a hole, as at pla, the plain twin; sp could take any part, so the parts it reaches are one
# hole part of the hole balance, possibly ania_tomek's only, and fix's take reaches it: no RUN-PLACE.  q1: the three
# reads are the balance's hole (spend), as pla's is.  q2: fix took 150.00 (a_fix carried through) from parts whose
# every possible label is ania_tomek's.  Before: `fix takes acc below 0` (the hole outflow left the parts as they were).
=== m.tally
model t10
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-15
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source src "test"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

kind couples: parties

kind persons: parties

kind cash_accounts: place one min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(DUK)
  takes k for w order rank[k.owner]

kind plain_accounts: place one min 0

place acc: cash_accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place pla: plain_accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2000-01-01..

input spend: money DUK question "how much do we spend?"

input d_dep: date

input d_sp: date

input d_fix: date

input a_dep: money DUK

input a_fix: money DUK

def rank[p in parties]: int = ?"which money leaves first?" at reader

def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = (if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0)

move dep: transfers
  on d_dep
  at d_dep
  leg cash from world to acc amount a_dep

move dep2: transfers
  on d_dep
  at d_dep
  leg cash from world to pla amount a_dep

move sp: transfers
  on d_sp
  at d_sp
  leg cash from acc to world amount spend

move sp2: transfers
  on d_sp
  at d_sp
  leg cash from pla to world amount spend

move fix: transfers
  on d_fix
  at d_fix
  leg cash from acc to world amount a_fix

move fix2: transfers
  on d_fix
  at d_fix
  leg cash from pla to world amount a_fix

ask q1: bal(acc, 2025-04-30), bal(pla, 2025-04-30), bal(acc, 2025-03-31) of ania_tomek

ask q2: fix.cash.amount of ania_tomek

version cast
  cite src
  known 2021-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1991-03-14..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1989-07-02..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2016-09-10..

version facts
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2021-01-01
  d_dep = 2025-02-01
  d_sp = 2025-03-01
  d_fix = 2025-04-01
  a_dep = 100.00
  a_fix = 150.00
=== expect
q1: (?"how much do we spend?" (spend), ?"how much do we spend?" (spend), ?"how much do we spend?" (spend))
...
q2: 150.00 DUK
...
